            "message": "Patch Set 3: Code-Review-1\n\ntoo much has been copy pasted from ibm/openpower-vpd-parser here.  I can't accept this without some rationale explaining why the existing frameworks aren't suitable."
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1596509144,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Andy_YF Wang",
                "email": "Andy_YF_Wang@wistron.com",
                "username": "AndyYFWang"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 3:\n\n(1 comment)\n\n> Patch Set 3: Code-Review-1\n> \n> too much has been copy pasted from ibm/openpower-vpd-parser here.  I can't accept this without some rationale explaining why the existing frameworks aren't suitable.\n\nHi Brad,\nI will need to write this bb file to start ibm-parser because Mihawk needs this parser to implement 250-soc VPD parsing, but Mihawk also needs openpower-parser to parse BMC's VPD data.\n\nWith the current situation of openpower-vpd-parser(https://github.com/openbmc/openpower-vpd-parser/blob/master/meson.build#L72), I found that only one parser (openpower-parser or ibm-parser) can be compiled. \nBecause of this, my solution is to write another bb file to compile ibm-parser so that openpower-parser and ibm-parser exist at the same time."
        },
